From bb7a647eb3bbfbec8f515cd5d2e390027367ae8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 17:07:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign the results dashboard with a validated color system

- Assign each TLS group a fixed categorical color (validated CVD-safe
  against both light and dark surfaces) instead of one flat blue for
  every bar, so identity is never lost across RTT/loss facets and
  filtering never repaints survivors.
- Add a legend, a proper hover/focus tooltip layer (value leads,
  larger hit targets, keyboard-accessible), and theme-aware CSS custom
  properties for light/dark instead of ad hoc hex and system colors.
- Fix bar marks to spec: capped thickness, rounded data-end/square
  baseline, nice-number axis ticks.
- Suppress per-bar labels once the view holds more than 12 bars (the
  full 36-condition view) to stop label collisions; the legend,
  tooltip, and table below stay reachable and carry the same values.
- Apply tabular-nums to table number columns.

Verified with rendered screenshots (light/dark, hover, keyboard focus,
dense view) and the dataviz skill's palette validator; all 21 existing
tests plus new coverage for the legend/tooltip markup pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
